<%# Faithful port of the legacy SPA `Hujah/card.js` — one feed card for a top-level hujah:
    header (tile avatar/handle/more-options), tappable body, the shared vote widget, and
    a counts footer (total votes · responses · live debate).

    HOOJAH 2026 (redesign Phase 1, Task 1.3) — mockup ~217-247. What moved from the
    Slice 9 shape:

    - `rounded-2xl` on the card. Slice 9's `ui/_card` header calls rounding a feed card
      "the one thing Card.prompt.md forbids outright" — that rule is this call site's
      SUPERSEDED, not the primitive's: `ds_card_classes` never bakes in a `rounded-*`
      utility (`CARD_BASE = "shadow bg-card"`), so `class: "rounded-2xl"` here is not a
      same-family override fight, just this card opting into the 2026 mockup's rounding
      while `ui/_card`'s other callers (menus aside, which already round via their own
      partial) stay square until they take their own redesign pass. (Task 1.4 revisits
      this rounding when a live debate is present — see that task's own note.)
    - The footer's vote-count glyph is `bar-chart-3` (was `bar-chart-2`) per the redesign
      spec; when `hujah.active_debate` is present the footer also carries a `swords`
      indicator and a "Jump in →" pill to the hujah — both omitted entirely, not
      hidden, when there is no active debate. No verified badge: this product has no
      `User#verified?` concept.

    DESIGN SYSTEM (Slice 9, Task 4.3, still true) —
    docs/design-system/components/hujah/HujahCard.prompt.md: "the primary unit of the
    product".

    - `data-testid="hujah-card"` goes through the card's `data:` local — which exists
      for exactly this attribute. Three specs select on it (spec/requests/hujahs_index_spec,
      spec/system/smoke_spec, spec/system/local_time_spec), so it is frozen, and
      `content_tag`'s dasherising reproduces it byte for byte.
    - The body is 18px `leading-snug` (`text-lg`) here and 20px (`text-xl`) on
      `hujahs/show` — the prompt's `size="detail"`. Do not unify them.

    The footer's hairline is `ui/_divider` rather than a `border-t` on the footer
    itself — the design system's "hairline `#f3f4f6` internal dividers" idiom. %>
<%= render layout: "ui/card",
      locals: {as: "article", data: {testid: "hujah-card"}, class: "mb-2 rounded-2xl"} do %>
  <%= render "hujahs/hujah_header", hujah: hujah %>

  <div class="px-4 pt-3 pb-0">
    <%= link_to hujah_path(hujah.slug), class: "block text-ink no-underline" do %>
      <div class="hujah-body text-lg leading-snug"><%= format_body(hujah.body) %></div>
    <% end %>
  </div>

  <%= render "hujahs/vote_bars",
        hujah: hujah,
        current_user_vote: hujah.current_user_vote(logged_in: user_signed_in?, current_user_id: current_user&.id) %>

  <%= render "ui/divider" %>
  <%# HujahCard.prompt.md: "the footer is always bar-chart-3 + total votes ·
      message-circle + response count". Always both, always that order; the swords
      indicator + Jump-in pill are additive, only when `hujah.active_debate` exists. %>
  <div class="px-4 py-2 flex items-center text-sm text-ink-2">
    <%= link_to hujah_path(hujah.slug), class: "flex items-center text-ink-2 no-underline" do %>
      <%= lucide_icon("bar-chart-3", class: "w-4 h-4") %>
      <span class="ml-1"><%= hujah.agree_count.to_i + hujah.neutral_count.to_i + hujah.disagree_count.to_i %></span>
      <span class="mx-2">·</span>
      <%= lucide_icon("message-circle", class: "w-4 h-4") %>
      <span class="ml-1"><%= hujah.children.size %></span>
    <% end %>

    <% if hujah.active_debate %>
      <span class="ml-3 flex items-center text-disagree" aria-label="Live debate on this hujah">
        <%= lucide_icon("swords", class: "w-4 h-4") %>
      </span>
      <%= link_to hujah_path(hujah.slug),
            class: "#{ds_button_classes(variant: :outline, tone: "primary", size: :sm)} ml-auto" do %>
        Jump in <%= lucide_icon("arrow-right", class: "w-3.5 h-3.5") %>
      <% end %>
    <% end %>
  </div>
<% end %>
